{"id":"G4816","lemma":"συλλέγω","transliteration":"sullegō","sayIt":"sullegō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to collect","meaning":"συλ-λέγω\n[in LXX chiefly for לָקַט ;]\nto bring together, collect, gather up: with accusative of thing(s), Mat.13:28-30; pass., Mat.13:40; with accusative, before ἀπό, Mat.7:16; id. before ἐκ, Mat.13:41, Luk.6:44; before εἰς, Mat.13:48.†\n(AS)","glosses":["grapes gathered","pull them up","pull","collect","collected","weed"],"count":8,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-7","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"Are grapes gathered","kjv":"Do men gather"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"pull them up","kjv":"nd gather"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":29,"renderings":{"bsb":"you pull","kjv":"while ye gather up"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":30,"renderings":{"bsb":"collect","kjv":"Gather ye together"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":40,"renderings":{"bsb":"are collected","kjv":"are gathered"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":41,"renderings":{"bsb":"they will weed","kjv":"they shall gather"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":48,"renderings":{"bsb":"and sorted","kjv":"and gathered"}},{"chapterId":"luk-6","v":44,"renderings":{"bsb":"are not gathered","kjv":"gather"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Matthew 7:16","note":"By their fruits you will know them. Do you gather grapes from thorns, or figs from thistles?","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 6:44","note":"For each tree is known by its own fruit. For people don’t gather figs from thorns, nor do they gather grapes from a bramble bush.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}